---
/*
 * `/data/smb-outlook-gap` — Korea's small-business outlook index against the lived one.
 * (seoulmarkets.com/data/smb-outlook-gap)
 *
 * ── Why this page (2026-10-12 17:1x · 5번) ───────────────────────────
 *   다섯 번째 데이터 지면이다. 오늘 두 번 고친 「안 쓴 축」 자가
 *   (이번엔 **의존까지 읽어**) 내놓은 22개에서 골랐다.
 *   ⛔ 짓기 전에 `check-이축으로-이미낸게있나` 를 돌렸다 — 다만 열쇠가 한글이라
 *     그 자가 거의 못 봤다(찾을 낱말 0개). 그래서 손으로도 훑었다.
 *
 *   잰 수가 드물다 —
 *   ```
 *     짝지은 149달 가운데 «149달» 전망이 체감보다 높다 — 100.0%
 *     중앙 21.3포인트 · 가장 큰 64.4(2020-03) · 가장 작은 1.2(2024-08)
 *     체감이 100 을 넘은 달은 «하나», 전망은 열다섯
 *   ```
 *
 * ── 🔴 What this page must not become ────────────────────────────────
 * 🔴 **「소상공인이 낙관한다」고 말하지 않는다.**
 *   전망 BSI 와 체감 BSI 가 «같은 질문»인지 우리는 모른다. 물음도 표본도 다를 수 있다.
 *   149/149 는 사람의 기분이 아니라 **두 자가 다른 것을 잰다는 뜻**일 수 있다.
 *   ⇒ 수를 내놓고, 무엇을 뜻하는지는 **보는 사람이 정한다.** 그것이 나침반이다.
 * ⛔ 「전망치를 믿지 마라」도 말하지 않는다. 치우친 자도 쓸모가 있다 —
 *   치우친 만큼을 알면 읽을 수 있다. 우리는 그 치우침을 재 줄 뿐이다.
 * ⛔ 못 짝지은 달을 0 으로 채우지 않는다.
 * ⛔ English only — 사장님 2026-08-05 「우리 손님은 영어권이다. 화면에 한국어를 안 낸다」.
 * ⛔ Numbers come from src/data/smb-outlook-gap.json, never typed by hand.
 * 🔴 Astro frontmatter (between the `---`) is TypeScript. JSX breaks the build.
 */
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { SITE_URL } from '../../consts';
import facts from '../../data/smb-outlook-gap.json';
import BuyBar from '../../components/BuyBar.astro';

const f = facts as any;
const N = (n: number | null | undefined) =>
  n == null ? '—' : Number(n).toLocaleString('en-GB');
const pct = (x: number | null | undefined, d = 1) =>
  x == null ? '—' : `${(Number(x) * 100).toFixed(d)}%`;
const pt = (n: number | null | undefined) =>
  n == null ? '—' : `${Number(n).toFixed(1)} pts`;
const 달 = (s: string | null | undefined) =>
  !s ? '—' : `${String(s).slice(0, 4)}-${String(s).slice(4, 6)}`;

const 벌어진달 = Array.isArray(f.벌어진달) ? f.벌어진달 : [];
const 좁은달 = Array.isArray(f.좁은달) ? f.좁은달 : [];
const 해마다 = Array.isArray(f.해마다) ? f.해마다 : [];
const 모자란해 = 해마다.filter((r: any) => !r.온전한가);
const 못짝 = (f.못짝지은것?.체감만 ?? 0) + (f.못짝지은것?.전망만 ?? 0);

const title = 'Korea’s small-business outlook has never once undershot';
const description =
  `Across ${N(f.짝수)} months, the forward-looking small-business index sat above the `
  + `lived one every single time — ${N(f.전망이높은달)} of ${N(f.짝수)}, median gap `
  + `${pt(f.중앙차)}. We publish the gap without claiming to know what causes it.`;
---

<Base title={title} description={description} canonical={`${SITE_URL}/data/smb-outlook-gap`}>
  <article class="wrap">
    <h1>{title}</h1>

    <p class="lead">
      Korea publishes two business-sentiment readings for small merchants each month: what
      the coming month is expected to look like, and what the month just lived through
      actually felt like. Both run on the same 100-point scale, where above 100 means
      improving. Lined up month by month from {달(f.첫달)} to {달(f.끝달)}, the
      forward-looking figure sat above the lived one
      {' '}<b>{N(f.전망이높은달)} times out of {N(f.짝수)}</b> — {pct(f.전망이높은몫)} — with a
      median gap of <b>{pt(f.중앙차)}</b>.
    </p>

    <div class="stats">
      <div class="stat"><b>{pct(f.전망이높은몫)}</b><span>months the outlook sat higher</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><b>{pt(f.중앙차)}</b><span>median gap</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><b>{pt(f.가장큰차)}</b><span>widest ({달(f.벌어진달?.[0]?.달)})</span></div>
      <div class="stat"><b>{N(f.체감이백넘은달)} / {N(f.짝수)}</b><span>months the lived index cleared 100</span></div>
    </div>

    <div class="warn">
      <p>
        <b>Read this as a property of two instruments, not of anyone's mood.</b> We do not
        know that the two indices put the same question to the same people. A reading of
        {' '}{N(f.전망이높은달)} out of {N(f.짝수)} in one direction, across twelve years and
        through a pandemic, is at least as likely to be how the pair is built as it is to
        be optimism. <b>This page measures the distance. It does not name the cause.</b>
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2>How wide, and when</h2>
    <p>
      The gap is not constant. It ran {pt(f.가장큰차)} at its widest in
      {' '}{달(f.벌어진달?.[0]?.달)} and {pt(f.가장작은차)} at its narrowest in
      {' '}{달(f.좁은달?.[0]?.달)}. A reader converting the forward index into an
      expectation of the lived one needs that spread, not just the average.
    </p>
    <div class="scroll">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Month</th>
            <th class="num">Outlook</th>
            <th class="num">Lived</th>
            <th class="num">Gap</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {벌어진달.map((r: any) => (
            <tr>
              <td>{달(r.달)}</td>
              <td class="num">{Number(r.전망).toFixed(1)}</td>
              <td class="num">{Number(r.체감).toFixed(1)}</td>
              <td class="num">{pt(r.차)}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
          <tr class="sep"><td colspan="4">— narrowest —</td></tr>
          {좁은달.map((r: any) => (
            <tr>
              <td>{달(r.달)}</td>
              <td class="num">{Number(r.전망).toFixed(1)}</td>
              <td class="num">{Number(r.체감).toFixed(1)}</td>
              <td class="num">{pt(r.차)}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>

    <h2>The level, not just the gap</h2>
    <p>
      On the shared scale, 100 is the line between improving and worsening. The lived index
      cleared it in <b>{N(f.체감이백넘은달)}</b> of {N(f.짝수)} months. The forward index
      cleared it in <b>{N(f.전망이백넘은달)}</b>. Whatever the gap means, the two series do
      not merely sit at different heights — they fall on opposite sides of the line that the
      scale itself defines as the interesting one.
    </p>

    <h2>Year by year</h2>
    <div class="scroll">
      <table>
        <thead>
          <tr>
            <th>Year</th>
            <th class="num">Median gap</th>
            <th class="num">Months</th>
            <th>Complete</th>
          </tr>
        </thead>
        <tbody>
          {해마다.map((r: any) => (
            <tr>
              <td>{r.해}</td>
              <td class="num">{pt(r.중앙차)}</td>
              <td class="num">{N(r.달수)}</td>
              <td class="dim">{r.온전한가 ? 'Yes' : 'Partial year'}</td>
            </tr>
          ))}
        </tbody>
      </table>
    </div>
    {모자란해.length > 0 && (
      <p class="note">
        {N(모자란해.length)} of these years hold fewer than twelve months — the series starts
        mid-year and ends mid-year. They are marked rather than placed beside full years as
        though equivalent.
      </p>
    )}
    {못짝 > 0 && (
      <p class="note">
        {N(못짝)} month{못짝 === 1 ? '' : 's'} appear in only one of the two series and are
        excluded from every figure above rather than filled in. The forward index runs one
        month further ahead than the lived one, which is what that exclusion is.
      </p>
    )}

    <h2 class="warn-h">What this page does not tell you</h2>
    <div class="warn">
      <ul>
        <li>
          <b>That the outlook is wrong.</b> Two indices can both be accurate measurements of
          two different things. We lined them up because they share a scale and a subject,
          not because we established that they share a question.
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>That you should discount the forward reading.</b> A consistently offset
          instrument is a usable one — arguably more usable than an erratic unbiased one.
          Knowing the offset is the point; deciding what to do with it is not ours.
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>Why the distance moves.</b> It widened to {pt(f.가장큰차)} in
          {' '}{달(f.벌어진달?.[0]?.달)} and narrowed to {pt(f.가장작은차)}. We counted the
          movement. We did not test a single explanation for it.
        </li>
        <li>
          <b>Anything about one business.</b> This is a survey aggregate across a sector.
          It is a statistic, not a statement about any merchant.
        </li>
      </ul>
    </div>

    <p class="note">
      Source: {f._출처}. Table {f._표}. Units: {f._단위}. Collected {f._뽑은날}. Every figure
      on this page is computed at build time from <code>smb-outlook-gap.json</code> by
      {' '}<code>scripts/measure-smb-outlook-gap.mjs</code>; none is transcribed by hand.
    </p>

    <BuyBar />
  </article>
</Base>

<style>
  .wrap { max-width: 56rem; margin: 0 auto; padding: 1.5rem 1rem 3rem; }
  h1 { font-size: 1.6rem; line-height: 1.25; margin: 0 0 .6rem; }
  h2 { font-size: 1.12rem; margin: 1.8rem 0 .5rem; }
  h2.warn-h { color: var(--warn, #9a3412); }
  .lead { font-size: 1rem; line-height: 1.65; margin: 0 0 1.2rem; }
  p { line-height: 1.65; }
  .stats {
    display: grid; gap: .6rem; margin: 1rem 0 1.4rem;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(9rem, 1fr));
  }
  .stat { padding: .7rem .8rem; border: 1px solid var(--line, #e5e5e5); border-radius: 6px; }
  .stat b { display: block; font-size: 1.25rem; line-height: 1.2; }
  .stat span { font-size: .78rem; color: var(--muted, #666); }
  .warn {
    padding: .8rem .95rem; border-left: 4px solid var(--accent, #0f4c81);
    background: color-mix(in srgb, var(--accent, #0f4c81) 6%, transparent);
    margin: 1rem 0;
  }
  .warn p { margin: 0; }
  .note { font-size: .85rem; color: var(--muted, #555); }
  .scroll { overflow-x: auto; }
  table { border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; font-size: .85rem; margin: .6rem 0; }
  th, td { text-align: left; padding: .45rem .55rem; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line, #eee); }
  th { font-weight: 650; white-space: nowrap; }
  td.num, th.num { text-align: right; white-space: nowrap; font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums; }
  td.dim, span.dim { color: var(--muted, #666); white-space: nowrap; }
  tr.sep td {
    text-align: center; font-size: .78rem; color: var(--muted, #666);
    padding: .5rem; border-bottom: 0;
  }
  ul { line-height: 1.65; padding-left: 1.2rem; }
  ul li { margin-bottom: .45rem; }
  code { font-size: .9em; }
  @media (prefers-color-scheme: dark) {
    .stat { border-color: #333; }
    h2.warn-h { color: #fdba74; }
    td.dim, span.dim, .note, .stat span, tr.sep td { color: #aaa; }
  }
</style>
